- Every reply to Ashok ends with **YOUR ACTION** (one concrete next step) and **DECISION** (one YES/NO or A/B).

## Open source first

- Before building a subsystem from scratch, recommend a quality OSS or free-tier product and only write glue.
- Do not put analytics/event warehouses on the invitations Supabase project.
- Alert Ashok when a request would reinvent a solved wheel.

## Source safety

- Commit locally only when Ashok asks.
- Ask twice before `git push`. Never force-push.
- Remote is `hardwin/findmyinvite` on `main` only.

## Production deploy

- Do not flip GitHub `ENABLE_PRODUCTION_DEPLOY` without Ashok's word.
- After a gated production push, set it back to `false`.
- Push to `main` currently verifies only; it does not auto-deploy production.

